    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 15th with a clear focal point in **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, who earns our daily top-tier rating at 80.98. The combination of a favorable matchup against Lorenzen and a massive boost from the leadoff spot makes him our essential engine for today\u2019s SB-heavy strategy. While **Junior Caminero** also projects strongly (71.38), his success hinges on capitalizing on Lauer\u2019s 4.63 xERA, making him the premier power-side anchor of the middle order. **Trea Turner** remains an elite play at 63.89; notably, the \"Slow SP Delivery\" metric against Gusto provides a hidden floor for **Trea Turner** to swipe bases, which is the high-leverage edge we prioritize in our roster construction.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical headwinds today, specifically with **Yordan Alvarez**, whose raw 55.68 score is hampered by a significant 19% penalty due to the skill level of Anderson. While **Yordan Alvarez** possesses an elite 0.453 xwOBA that keeps him in the lineup, his upside is capped compared to the favorable platoon splits we are seeing elsewhere. **Dillon Dingler** sits at the bottom of our active threshold (41.43), primarily due to a 15% penalty regarding his platoon disadvantage against Teng; he remains our only real candidate to be swapped should a late-breaking lineup change favor a stronger platoon option like **Luke Raley** or **Nelson Velazquez** from the bench.\n\nRegarding the bench, **Carson Benge** (48.31) narrowly edged out the rest of the reserve corps, despite facing the stiffest challenge of the day in Burns. We considered rotating in **Josh Smith** or **Casey Schmitt** to mitigate the risk of Burns\u2019 elite 3.04 xERA, but the combination of the leadoff slot and the 7% platoon boost for **Carson Benge** provided just enough mathematical weight to keep him in the starting nine. We continue to monitor the status of **Christian Yelich** and **Caleb Durbin**, both of whom are currently unavailable; we remain hopeful that **Hyeseong Kim** and **Rece Hinds** can force their way back into the major league plans, as their current status in the minors continues to limit our depth during this high-intensity stretch.",
